Good. Now I have the project structure. Let me plan and implement the components.

## Component Plan

```
ApplyPage                    (page — owns all form state, orchestrates steps)
├── StepIndicator            (shows step progress bar)
├── PersonalInfoStep         (step 1)
├── WorkHistoryStep          (step 2)
│   └── WorkEntryForm        (single work entry)
├── ReferencesStep           (step 3)
│   └── ReferenceForm        (single reference)
├── CoverLetterStep          (step 4)
└── ReviewStep               (step 5)
```

Now I'll implement these in order: first the data models and service interface, then the leaf components, followed by the step components, the step indicator, and finally the main ApplyPage that ties everything together. I'm using mutable model classes for form binding since records are immutable.

I'll organize everything under the project namespace with models in a dedicated folder and components structured under the Apply page directory.

```

